---
import ProviderPlaybookTemplate from '../components/ProviderPlaybookTemplate.astro';
const data = {
 "kind": "connect",
 "name": "Squarespace",
 "title": "How to Connect a Domain to Squarespace",
 "description": "Point your custom domain to Squarespace: exact records, method choice, and verification.",
 "intro": "Connecting an existing domain to Squarespace takes two DNS changes done carefully. Here is the exact method and the verification step.",
 "steps": [
  [
   "Start the connection",
   "Squarespace, Settings, Domains: Use a domain I own, enter it, choose Connect."
  ],
  [
   "Publish the records",
   "Squarespace shows verification CNAME plus four A records (198.185.159.x range); add all in your DNS host."
  ],
  [
   "Verify",
   "Back in Squarespace, click Refresh; SSL follows automatically after verification."
  ]
 ],
 "quirk": "Squarespace requires all four A records plus the verification CNAME; adding only one A record gives intermittent site loads.",
 "faqs": [
  [
   "Nameservers instead?",
   "Squarespace offers a nameserver option (use squarespace.domains NS); the CNAME/A-record pointing method keeps your current DNS host, which is usually better."
  ],
  [
   "How long do DNS changes take in Squarespace?",
   "The provider serves new values quickly, but resolvers keep old answers until each record's TTL expires. Verify live values with the record lookup, then watch the propagation checker until resolvers agree."
  ],
  [
   "Where do I find Squarespace's nameservers?",
   "This playbook's nameservers guide covers the exact location. They are the delegation pair your registrar must point at for Squarespace to be authoritative."
  ],
  [
   "Should I lower TTL before changing records in Squarespace?",
   "Yes, for anything planned: set TTL to 300 seconds at least one old-TTL cycle ahead, make the change, confirm propagation, then restore the TTL."
  ],
  [
   "Can I keep email with one provider and DNS in Squarespace?",
   "Yes: DNS host and mail provider are independent. Publish the mail provider's MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records in Squarespace, and keep those records unproxied."
  ]
 ],
 "related": [
  [
   "DNS record types reference",
   "/dns-records/"
  ],
  [
   "TTL explained",
   "/what-is-ttl-in-dns/"
  ]
 ]
};
---
<ProviderPlaybookTemplate data={data} />
